    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 **56 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**, including the new `Cp45Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `salutation` feature end-to-end, following the project's established pattern for derived owner fields (like `locality`, `membershipPoints`, `checkDigit`):\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional write field `title` to the `OwnerFields` schema and a read-only derived field `salutation` to the `Owner` schema. These regenerate into `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` at build time.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** (entity) \u2014 added a persisted `title` column with getter/setter, and a `@Transient getSalutation()` that returns `title + \" \" + lastName`, or just `lastName` when the title is absent/blank.\n\n3. **DB schemas** (hsqldb, h2, postgres, mysql) \u2014 added the `title` column to the `owners` table. The test profile uses hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`, so the column had to be declared explicitly.\n\nNo mapper changes were needed: MapStruct auto-maps `title` (both directions) and `salutation` (`Owner.getSalutation()` \u2192 `OwnerDto.salutation`) by matching property names. The `title` flows in through `ValidateOwnerFields` (which republishes the whole body) and `BuildOwner`, gets persisted by `SaveOwner`, and `salutation` is computed at read time on the `GET`.",
